@bank all
// Head writer 0607: Say hello and Talk a while (the social engineer's, plan-0607 "Talking"). Keys in content/keys-0607.md.
// hello: their answer when you Say hello (the quick corridor nod; once a day). talk.*: Talk a while, 15 ship minutes:
// a start line, then a topic (open, a few "more" lines every few seconds, an ask, your three replies, their answer),
// filler when a topic runs dry, and an end or stop line. talk.go.*: they really have to be somewhere.
// Replies (talk.<topic>.reply.*) are TEXTS: your words on the buttons, no voice tokens. listen = curious, share =
// about you, cheer = light. The one that matches their voice card's needs: gives +2. None is wrong, so every answer
// is glad of the reply. {hobby} is the roster's phrase ("reading old paper novels"); {home} their home ("Marra Station").

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Say hello
== hello
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. You're the new one, aren't you? Welcome aboard.
- {hi}. Settling in all right?
- Oh, {hi}. I've seen you about. Nice to meet you properly.
- {hi}. Don't worry, nobody knows where anything is for a week.   #funny
- Hello, new face. You'll be fine. Everyone's friendly here.
- {hi}. If you get lost, follow the smell of toast to the mess.   #funny
? tier=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. Getting the hang of the place?
- Oh, {hi}. Good to see you again.
- {hi}. Still finding your way? You're doing well.
- {hi}, {nick}. Busy day?
- Hey, it's you. How's the Wren treating you?
- {hi}. Found the good tea yet? Lounge, top shelf.
? tier=colleague
- {hi}, {nick}. Same time tomorrow?
- There you are. {hi}.
- {hi}. You look like you know where you're going today.   #funny
- {hi}, {nick}. Good shift?
- Oh, {hi}. I was just thinking I hadn't seen you.
- {hi}. Off anywhere nice?
? tier=friend
- {hi}, {nick}. Made my day, that.   #warm
- Oh good, it's you. {hi}.
- {hi}! Come and find me later. I've got news.
- {nick}! I was hoping I'd see you.   #warm
- {hi}. You look well. The Wren suits you.
- There's my favourite new hand. {hi}.   #funny
? tier=close
- {hi}, {nick}. Always good to see your face.   #warm
- Oh, it's you. Everything's better already.   #warm
- {nick}! Sit with me at dinner?
- {hi}. Don't go far. I want a proper catch-up.   #warm
? time:morning
- Morning. Don't talk to me till tea. Kidding. {hi}.   #funny
- {hi}. Early one, isn't it?
? time:evening
- {hi}. Shift's done. Best part of the day, this.
- Evening, {nick}. Doing anything nice tonight?
? time:night
- {hi}. Shouldn't you be asleep? Shouldn't I?   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Talk a while: starting and stopping
== talk.start
- Got a few minutes? Go on, then.
- Oh, a proper chat. Lovely. I've got time.
- Sure. Pull up a bit of wall.   #funny
- I'd like that. Go on, what's new?
- Talk? Always. Tell me everything.
- Course. I was hoping someone would stop.   #warm
? tier>=friend
- For you? I've always got time.   #warm
- Oh good. I've been saving things up to tell you.

== talk.sit
- Sit down, sit down. There's room.
- Grab a seat. This one's comfy, I checked.   #funny
- Oh, have a seat. I was getting bored of me.   #funny
- Sit. Get comfy. I'm not going anywhere.

== talk.filler
- Anyway. What was I saying? Oh, never mind. It's nice, this.
- Funny how quiet it gets in here at this time.
- I like a chat. People don't stop enough.
- Is it me, or does the ship hum louder in the evening?
- You're easy to talk to. Has anyone told you that?   #warm
- Mm. Where was I? Doesn't matter.
- I could do this all evening. Shame about bedtime.   #funny
- You've got a good laugh. Use it more.   #warm
- Sorry, I'm rambling. Stop me if I ramble.   #funny
- Tea would make this perfect. Next time, tea.

== talk.end
- That was nice. Let's do it again soon.   #warm
- Right, I've talked your ear off. Thanks for listening.
- Good chat. I feel better for that.   #warm
- Same time tomorrow? Only half joking.   #funny
- That's the best part of my day sorted. Off you go.   #warm
- Thanks, {nick}. I needed that.
? tier>=friend
- You're good company, you know that? Go on, scoot.   #warm

== talk.stop
- Oh, off you go? Catch you later.
- Another time, then. No rush.
- Right you are. Finish this another day.
- Go on, I'll keep the rest for next time.
- No worries. I'll be here. Probably.   #funny

== talk.go.shift
- Shift in five. Catch me later?
- Oh, look at the time. I'm on soon. Sorry.
- I'd love to, but my shift's starting. Another time?
- Can't stop, shift's calling. Later, yes?
- Got to go, I'm on in ten. Find me after?

== talk.go.bed
- I'm off to bed. Tomorrow, though?
- Can't keep my eyes open. Talk tomorrow?
- Bedtime for me. Night, {nick}.
- I'd only yawn at you. Tomorrow, I promise.   #funny

== talk.go.trad
- I'm running {trad} in a minute. Come along?
- Can't stop, {trad}'s on and it's mine to start.
- Sorry, {trad}. I'm the one who opens it. Come with me?

== talk.go.call
- I've a call home booked. Another time?
- Booth's booked for me in a minute. Sorry, {nick}.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the card's words (texts)
== talk.button.hello
- Say hello

== talk.button.talk
- Talk a while

== talk.button.stop
- Stop

== talk.done.hello
- Said hello today

== talk.done.talk
- Talked today

== roster.tab.all
- Everyone

== roster.tab.known
- People I know

== roster.friends
- Friends ({n})

== roster.acq
- Acquaintances ({n})

== roster.met
- Met ({n})

== roster.none
- Nobody yet. Say hello to someone.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: hobby
== talk.hobby.open
- I've been {hobby} again. Can't stop, honestly.
- Did you know I'm into {hobby}? Well, now you do.   #funny
- I spent all last night {hobby}. Worth it.
- People think {hobby} is boring. People are wrong.   #funny
== talk.hobby.more
- It's the one hour where my head goes quiet.
- I started it to pass the time. Now I make time for it.
- My bunkmates have stopped asking. That's how you know it's serious.   #funny
- I'm not even good at it. That's not the point.
- There's always one more thing to try. That's the hook.
- Best part of the evening, that. Nobody needs anything from me.
== talk.hobby.ask
- Have you got a thing? Something you do just because?
- What do you do when your shift's done?
== talk.hobby.reply.listen
- How did you get into it?
== talk.hobby.reply.share
- I'm still finding mine. I might try a few.
== talk.hobby.reply.cheer
- Teach me. I'll be terrible.
== talk.hobby.ans.listen
- Someone showed me, years back. Now I can't put it down.   #warm
- Bored on a long trip, mostly. Best boredom I ever had.
== talk.hobby.ans.share
- Try a few. Drawing, puzzles, the stars. One will stick.
- Good. Take your time. It finds you, usually.   #warm
== talk.hobby.ans.cheer
- Terrible's how everyone starts. I'll hold you to it.   #funny
- Deal. Bring patience. And snacks.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: home
== talk.home.open
- I was thinking about {home} today. No reason.
- Something in the mess smelt like {home}. Took me right back.
- Got a letter from {home}. Nothing much in it. Read it three times.   #warm
- Have you ever been to {home}? You'd like it. Probably.
== talk.home.more
- It's the sky I miss. Silly, out here with all these stars.
- You don't notice the little things till you're gone.
- My street had a bakery on the corner. I could find it blindfold.
- It's funny. I wanted to leave so much. Now I talk about it all the time.   #funny
- The Wren's home too, now. Both at once. Is that odd?
- I'll go back on leave one day. It'll all be smaller.
== talk.home.ask
- Where's home for you, then? What's it like?
- Do you miss home yet? Be honest.
== talk.home.reply.listen
- What do you miss most about it?
== talk.home.reply.share
- I miss it. More than I thought I would.
== talk.home.reply.cheer
- Better bakeries than the Wren?
== talk.home.ans.listen
- The noise, oddly. Doors, voices, rain. The ship's too polite.
- The people, mostly. And the bread. Mostly the bread.   #funny
== talk.home.ans.share
- That's normal. It gets softer. Never quite goes.   #warm
- Me too, at first. Call home. It really helps.
== talk.home.ans.cheer
- Don't let Brennan hear you. But yes. Much better.   #funny
- Nobody beats Brennan. Don't tell home I said that.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: day
== talk.day.open
- What a day. I'll tell you about it if you've got the patience.   #funny
- Today was one of the good ones. Everything just worked.
- I've had a funny sort of day. Not bad. Funny.
- Long day. Better now I've sat down.
== talk.day.more
- Started with cold tea. Should've known.   #funny
- Someone said thank you, out of nowhere. Kept me going all afternoon.   #warm
- I fixed one thing and three more broke. Typical.   #funny
- Dinner was good, though. Dinner's always good.
- I ran about all morning, then sat still all afternoon.
- Nothing went wrong. Strangely tiring, that.
== talk.day.ask
- What about you? How was yours?
- Go on, your turn. Good day or bad day?
== talk.day.reply.listen
- What was the best bit?
== talk.day.reply.share
- Mine was busy. I learned a lot, though.
== talk.day.reply.cheer
- At least it's over. Dinner time.
== talk.day.ans.listen
- This, honestly. Sitting down with someone nice.   #warm
- Dinner. It's always dinner. I'm simple like that.   #funny
== talk.day.ans.share
- That's the best kind. You'll be teaching us soon.
- Busy and learning. That's a good day, that is.
== talk.day.ans.cheer
- Exactly. Dinner fixes most things.   #funny
- Right. Whatever's on, I'm having two.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: work
== talk.work.open
- Work's been odd this week. Good odd, mostly.
- I'm getting better at my job. Don't tell anyone, they'll give me more.   #funny
- There's a thing at work I can't stop thinking about.
- My boss said "well done" today. I'm still floating.   #warm
== talk.work.more
- Everyone here's good at what they do. Makes you want to keep up.
- Some days it's all small jobs. I like those, secretly.
- The trick is to ask. Nobody minds. They just like being asked.
- I made a mistake last month. Fixed it. Nobody shouted. That's the Wren.
- One day I'll run the place. Or a bit of it. A corner.   #funny
== talk.work.ask
- How's Works treating you? Calder working you hard?
- Are you liking the job so far?
== talk.work.reply.listen
- What's the best part of your job?
== talk.work.reply.share
- I like it. Still learning where everything goes.
== talk.work.reply.cheer
- I've fixed a lamp. I'm basically an expert.
== talk.work.ans.listen
- When it all runs and nobody notices. That's the job, really.
- The people. And the days when something hard finally works.
== talk.work.ans.share
- Everyone's still learning that. Even the old hands.
- You'll know it by heart soon. Then it gets fun.
== talk.work.ans.cheer
- An expert! I'll send all my lamps your way.   #funny
- Lamp expert. Put it on your door.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: food
== talk.food.open
- Did you have the {dish}? I'm still thinking about it.
- I'd do anything for a proper bun right now. Anything.   #funny
- Brennan's cooking something new. I can smell it from here.
- What's your favourite thing from the mess so far?
== talk.food.more
- I always go back for seconds. Brennan pretends not to see.   #funny
- Soup day is the best day. That's not up for debate.
- Home cooking was better. Don't tell Brennan.   #funny
- I tried to cook once, on leave. Never again.   #funny
- The garden lot bring fresh herbs up. You can taste it.
== talk.food.ask
- What do you miss eating most?
- Would you rather breakfast or dinner? Forever.
== talk.food.reply.listen
- What's the best thing you've eaten aboard?
== talk.food.reply.share
- I miss proper bread. Fresh from the oven.
== talk.food.reply.cheer
- Breakfast. Forever. Toast is life.
== talk.food.ans.listen
- Brennan's stew on a cold night. Changed my life.   #warm
- Harvest supper. The whole ship eats together. Wait till you see it.
== talk.food.ans.share
- Brennan bakes on Saturdays. Get there early. Trust me.
- Fresh bread. Oh, you've done it now. I'm hungry.   #funny
== talk.food.ans.cheer
- Toast is life. Finally, someone gets it.   #funny
- Bold. Correct, but bold.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: news (ship news)
== talk.news.open
- Have you heard? There's always something going round.
- Bit of news from the ship. Want to hear it?
- Something's going round the mess. Don't know if it's true.
== talk.news.more
- News moves faster than the lift on this ship.   #funny
- Half of it's true. The other half's more fun.   #funny
- I heard it in the tea queue, so it's half made up.   #funny
- Check your Mail. The good stuff's in there.
- Someone always knows before the notice goes up.
== talk.news.ask
- What have you heard, then? Anything good?
- Do you read the news on your device?
== talk.news.reply.listen
- Go on, what's the latest?
== talk.news.reply.share
- I don't know anything yet. Still the new one.
== talk.news.reply.cheer
- I only listen to rumours. Much more fun.
== talk.news.ans.listen
- Nothing big. Someone's moving bunks. Big news, here.   #funny
- The delivery's due Wednesday. That's about it. Thrilling, I know.   #funny
== talk.news.ans.share
- Stick with me. You'll know everything by Friday.
- You'll be telling me things by next week.
== talk.news.ans.cheer
- Me too. Truth is so boring.   #funny
- A rumour's just news that hasn't happened yet.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: tradition
== talk.tradition.open
- Are you going to {trad}? I'm going.
- {trad}'s coming up. It's one of my favourites.
- I never miss {trad}. Well, almost never.
== talk.tradition.more
- That's the thing about the Wren. There's always something on.
- You don't have to go to everything. Pick the ones you like.
- My first week, I went to all of them. I was so tired.   #funny
- Best way to meet people, honestly. Just turn up.
- Some nights there are two at once. You just pick one.
== talk.tradition.ask
- Have you been to any yet? Which one?
- Which ones are you going to try?
== talk.tradition.reply.listen
- Which one's your favourite?
== talk.tradition.reply.share
- Not yet. I'm a bit nervous, honestly.
== talk.tradition.reply.cheer
- All of them. I'll sleep next week.
== talk.tradition.ans.listen
- Observatory night. Lying on the floor looking up. Can't beat it.   #warm
- Tiles night. I'm not good, but I'm loud.   #funny
== talk.tradition.ans.share
- Come with me, then. I'll introduce you round.   #warm
- Don't be. Nobody minds a new face. They like it.
== talk.tradition.ans.cheer
- That's the spirit. Then the tiredness. Then the spirit again.   #funny
- Good plan. Bad plan. Do it anyway.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: crew (a crewmate)
== talk.crew.open
- Do you know {friend}? You'd get on.
- {friend} did the funniest thing this morning.   #funny
- Have you met {friend} yet? You should.
== talk.crew.more
- {friend} looked after me when I was new. I owe them one.
- We sit together most dinners. Come and join us.
- Everyone's got a story on this ship. Ask and you'll see.
- People look out for each other here. It's nice.
- I knew nobody when I came. Now look.
== talk.crew.ask
- Who've you got to know so far?
- Have you made any friends yet? Apart from me.   #funny
== talk.crew.reply.listen
- How did you two meet?
== talk.crew.reply.share
- A few people. Everyone's been kind.
== talk.crew.reply.cheer
- You. You're my only friend. No pressure.
== talk.crew.ans.listen
- Same bunk room, first week. Never looked back.   #warm
- We both got lost on Deck 2 once. Bonded over it.   #funny
== talk.crew.ans.share
- Kind's the Wren's whole thing. You'll fit right in.   #warm
- Good. Keep going. Everyone here's worth knowing.
== talk.crew.ans.cheer
- An honour. I'll try to be worth it.   #funny
- Ha! I'll share you round. You'll have ten by Friday.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: ship (the Wren herself)
== talk.ship.open
- I love this old ship. Don't tell her, she'll get big-headed.   #funny
- Have you been up to the observatory yet? You must.
- Listen. You hear that hum? That's the Wren, thinking.
== talk.ship.more
- She creaks at night. You stop hearing it after a week.
- There's a window on Deck 3 where the stars just pour past.
- Every deck smells different. Five is oil. Three is toast.   #funny
- I still find corners I've never seen. After all this time.
- She's old, but she's kind. Like a good boot.   #funny
== talk.ship.ask
- What do you think of her so far? The Wren?
- Found a favourite spot aboard yet?
== talk.ship.reply.listen
- Where's your favourite spot?
== talk.ship.reply.share
- I like her. She feels lived in.
== talk.ship.reply.cheer
- She's lovely. Bit far from the shops.   #funny
== talk.ship.ans.listen
- The lounge windows, late. Just me and the stars.   #warm
- The garden. It smells like rain in there.
== talk.ship.ans.share
- Lived in. That's it exactly. She's a home.   #warm
- She is. Everyone leaves a little bit of themselves.
== talk.ship.ans.cheer
- The crew store's a shop! Sort of. It has socks.   #funny
- No shops. Fewer things to buy. More money for drinks.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- topic: plans (the future, small)
== talk.plans.open
- I've been thinking about what I'll do next year.
- I've got a plan. A small one. Want to hear it?
- One day I'd like to see the bridge. Just once. Properly.
== talk.plans.more
- Maybe a course. Maybe nothing. It's nice to think about.
- First, though, I want to finish this scarf. Long-term goal.   #funny
- I keep a list. It's mostly food I want to try.   #funny
- Small steps, my gran said. She was usually right.
- I'm in no rush. The Wren's a good place to be for now.
== talk.plans.ask
- What about you? Where do you see yourself in a year?
- Got any plans, big or small?
== talk.plans.reply.listen
- What's the dream, then?
== talk.plans.reply.share
- I want to be good at this job. Really good.
== talk.plans.reply.cheer
- Plans? I'm planning dinner.
== talk.plans.ans.listen
- Running my own section. Or my own kettle. Either.   #funny
- Something of my own. Small, but mine.   #warm
== talk.plans.ans.share
- You will be. I can tell already.   #warm
- That's a good one. Stick with it.
== talk.plans.ans.cheer
- Now that's a plan I can get behind.   #funny
- Best plan on the ship. What's on tonight?
